# =============================================================================
# Environment Variables & Secrets - SECURITY CRITICAL
# =============================================================================
# Two-file system for environment variables:
#
# 1. .zshrc_envvars (IGNORED - contains SENSITIVE data)
#    - API keys, tokens, secrets, passwords
#    - Plain text storage with chmod 600
#    - Never committed to git
#
# 2. .zshrc_envvars_insecure (TRACKED - contains NON-SENSITIVE data)
#    - AWS regions, profiles, default configurations
#    - Safe to share with team via git
#    - Despite "_insecure" in name, this file is intentionally tracked
#    - Name indicates "insecure to store secrets here" not "ignored by git"
#
# IMPORTANT: The wildcard pattern *_insecure* was intentionally removed
# to allow .zshrc_envvars_insecure to be tracked. This is by design.
# =============================================================================

.zshrc_envvars
.env
.env.local
.env.production
.env.staging
**/secrets/
private/
secret.*

